      <p>The pivotal moment in mobile forensics came in 2016 with the San Bernardino terrorist attack case. The FBI
        demanded Apple create a backdoor into an iPhone — Apple refused, citing user privacy. This standoff forced
        forensics agencies to develop advanced bypass techniques, fundamentally reshaping the landscape of mobile
        investigation.</p>
