    <div class="section-block" id="s3">
      <h2 class="section-title">3. Types of Mobile Forensic Extraction</h2>
      <p>Data extraction from mobile devices is classified by depth and invasiveness. Think of it like peeling layers of
        an onion — each layer requires more skill and risk but reveals more data.</p>

      <!-- Pyramid SVG -->
      <div class="diagram-wrap">
        <svg width="100%" viewBox="0 0 680 340" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img">
          <title>Extraction Methods Pyramid</title>
          <desc>Pyramid diagram showing five levels of mobile forensic extraction from manual to chip-off</desc>
          <!-- Level 5 - Manual (bottom) -->
          <polygon points="40,300 640,300 580,248 100,248" fill="#e8f0fb" stroke="#1a2f4e" stroke-width="0.5"></polygon>
          <text x="340" y="280" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'Source Serif 4',serif" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="#1a2f4e">Manual Extraction</text>
          <text x="340" y="296" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'JetBrains Mono',monospace" font-size="10" fill="#3d3d5a">Screen photography / direct UI reading — slowest, least data</text>
          <!-- Level 4 -->
